TYPES.md §3.4, §4.2, DECISIONS 334: a lambda parameter named `it` inside a predicate hides the
predicate's `it`, so it gets the ordinary §4.1/§4.2 treatment: against an enum with a member `it`,
it is ambiguous (E2101).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local enum G { it, other }

local let gs: [G] = [other]

local type A1 = G where gs.any(it => it == it)
-- findings.txt --
error[E2101]  a/a.canon:7:44
  it is ambiguous: G.it or the parameter it; write it qualified

